'''Nueva Cuenca''' ({{Literal translation|new basin}}) is a barrio and [[Planned communities in Balisca|planned community]] situated on the [[Tidal Basin]] in southern [[Hisbanya]], within the [[Castejón Metropolis]]. 

The area is the site of a large-scale [[W:Redevelopment|redevelopment]] and [[W:Urban renewal|urban renewal]] program that is being planned, funded, and constructed under a set of agreements amongst the borough ([[Cantons of Balisca|canton]]) of Hisbanya, the [[Metropolitan Council of Castejón|Metropolitan Council]], and [[Autoridad de Transporte Metropolitano|Metropolitan Transportation Authority]] (ATM). 

The [[W:YIMBY|YIMBY]]-development program is part of a major [[W:Rezoning|rezoning]] and upzoning of Hisbanya as part of the [[Casajuan Plan|Casajuan Initiative]], also including the extension of the [[Castejón Metro]]'s 2 and 5​ lines to a new metro station at 34th Street and 11th Avenue, expansion of pedestrian and cycling infrastructure, and [[W:Greening|greening]]. The various components are being planned by [[Hisbanya Council of Urban Planning]] and [[Castejón Socioeconomic Development Cooperative]]. 

